   "captions_sha256": "9ec08a8670e5a98e66f70cee0700871b57fd0dba9bff437b742f430128a198b3",
   "created_at": "2026-11-24T03:16:40Z",
   "description": "Astronauts patched NASA's NICER telescope on the space station after sunlight leaked in through damaged shields. The patch worked, but a motor failed, and in November 2026 NASA shut NICER down anyway. Here is how the spacewalk repair was built, rehearsed and done.\n\nIn this episode:\n0:00 A space telescope that leaked light\n0:10 What NICER is\n0:35 The May 2023 light leak\n0:48 Never designed to be repaired\n1:00 A patch shaped like a slice of pie\n1:22 Rehearsal and the spacewalk repair\n1:52 Fixing the rest with electronics\n2:08 The motor that failed\n2:19 NICER shuts down\n\nSources:\n- NASA, NICER status updates: https://www.nasa.gov/missions/station/nicer-status-updates/\n- NASA, \"Astronauts To Patch Up NASA's NICER Telescope\": https://science.nasa.gov/missions/station/iss-research/nicer/astronauts-to-patch-up-nasas-nicer-telescope/\n- NASA, \"Repair Kit for NASA's NICER Mission Heading to Space Station\": https://science.nasa.gov/missions/station/iss-research/nicer/repair-kit-for-nasas-nicer-mission-heading-to-space-station/\n\nFootage: NASA via the Scientific Visualization Studio: https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/14678 , https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/14679 , https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/14680 , https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/14603 , https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/14609 , https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/14610 , https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/14819 . Public domain; NASA does not endorse this video. Underwater shots are training at NASA's Neutral Buoyancy Laboratory in Houston, not the spacewalk itself (labelled on screen). NICER-in-orbit shots are NASA animation. Charts: NEXORA.\nNarration: the channel creator's own voice, generated with ElevenLabs voice cloning.\n\n#NICER #NASA #Spacewalk #NEXORA",
